From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] cell64lv2: raise the branch cost to 8

rs6000.h:1000 sets BRANCH_COST to 3: "roughly the average cost of an
unscheduled conditional branch", tuned for an out-of-order POWER core.
The Cell PPU is in-order with a long pipeline: a mispredicted branch
costs more than on the cores that default was set for, while the
branch-free substitutes the middle end can generate (if-conversion,
conditional moves, count/sel/shift idioms) are no harder to issue here
than a taken branch.  With BRANCH_COST at 3 the if-converter
(ifcvt.cc), jump-eliminator (dojump.cc), expression matcher (expmed.cc)
and optabs (optabs.cc) see only a thin edge and keep the taken branch
when a branch-free idiom was available, so code that stores comparison
results, takes a min/max, or does branchy integer arithmetic was
compiled with the branch instead of the arithmetic/SEL/CTLZ form.

Raise BRANCH_COST to 8 in the target header.  cell64lv2.h is last in
the tm_file chain for powerpc64-ps3-elf, and defaults.h guards with
ifndef, so this override wins over rs6000.h's 3 and the 1-bit fallback.
LOGICAL_OP_NON_SHORT_CIRCUIT is left at its existing default
(0): it is a separate override for an orthogonal short-circuiting cost
issue and is not the right knob here.

Behaviour: slightly more code in branchy integer code; possibly a few
more registers live across a converted branch; small .text increase.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
@@ -577,3 +577,16 @@
    assumes it for malloc/calloc/realloc/strdup/strndup.  */
 #undef MALLOC_ABI_ALIGNMENT
 #define MALLOC_ABI_ALIGNMENT 128
+
+/* The Cell PPU is in-order with a long pipeline: a mispredicted
+   conditional branch costs more than the average-PowerPC value
+   rs6000.h sets (3, "roughly the average cost of an unscheduled
+   conditional branch") was tuned for, while the branch-free
+   substitutes the middle end can generate (if-conversion,
+   conditional moves, count/sel/shift idioms) are no harder to issue
+   here than a taken branch.  With BRANCH_COST at 3 the if-converter,
+   jump-eliminator and expression matcher keep the taken branch; raise
+   the promise to 8 so the branch-free form wins when it is available.
+   */
+#undef BRANCH_COST
+#define BRANCH_COST(speed_p, predictable_p) 8
